From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windowscodecs: the bitmap scaler's linear, cubic, Fant and high quality cubic modes resample

IWICBitmapScaler drew every interpolation mode as nearest neighbour ('unsupported mode 3', PDFgear at start; Fant is what WPF's DecodePixelWidth and many viewers ask for). For formats of 8-bit channels (24/32 bpp BGR/RGB, premultiplied or straight BGRA/RGBA, 8 bpp grey and alpha) the scaled image is now resampled, separably: linear (two taps), cubic (cubic convolution, a = -0.5), Fant (the covered source area, each pixel weighted by its coverage; linear when enlarging), high quality cubic (the cubic kernel stretched over the source area when reducing). Straight alpha weighs the colour. Other formats and nearest neighbour stay as they were.
---
--- a/dlls/windowscodecs/scaler.c
+++ b/dlls/windowscodecs/scaler.c
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <stdarg.h>
+#include <math.h>
 
 #define COBJMACROS
 
